  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 49\u2011year\u2011old man with a long history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension leading to progressive diabetic nephropathy. Over the past decade his chronic kidney disease has advanced from stage 1 to stage 4 (most recent onset 2022\u201111\u201110) and he is now listed as awaiting kidney transplantation (onset 2022\u201112\u201115). He has developed anemia (2022\u201110\u201127) and proteinuria (2018\u201107\u201126). Blood pressure remains suboptimally treated with low\u2011dose losartan and amlodipine. He continues to smoke daily, is obese (BMI\u202f\u2265\u202f30), and reports chronic low\u2011back pain managed with high\u2011dose opioid therapy (fentanyl patch, oxycodone/acetaminophen, extended\u2011release oxycodone). Opioid abuse was documented in 2017. He also experiences significant psychosocial stress, is a victim of intimate partner abuse, and has a criminal record. No recent laboratory values, vital signs, or cardiovascular imaging are available. The overall trajectory is marked by worsening renal function, uncontrolled metabolic risk factors, and high\u2011risk medication use while awaiting transplant evaluation.",
